  "text_sanskrit": "कर्मणः सुकृतस्याहुः सात्त्विकं निर्मलं फलम् । रजसस्तु फलं दुःखमज्ञानं तमसः फलम् ॥ १४-१६ ॥",
  "itrans": "karmaNaH sukR^itasyAhuH sAttvikaM nirmalaM phalam . rajasastu phalaM duHkhamaj~nAnaM tamasaH phalam .. 14-16 ..",
  "translation": "They declare that the fruit of the good deed is of the Satva nature and spotless, but the fruit of Rajas is misery, and the fruit of Tamas is the absence of knowledge. (16.) \nV. The good deed: of him who is born in the family of the wise. Misery: even happiness or pleasure mingled with misery becomes only misery. Absence of knowledge: includes all the effects of ignorance. (16.) \nA. The same is further explained.",
